Stellara worked with threads of pure shadow, pulling them tight across the heavens. But she grew lonely in her endless work, with only silence as her companion. One day, she wept, and her tears scattered across her canvas - each droplet transforming into a brilliant point of light.

Horrified at having ruined her perfect darkness, Stellara tried desperately to weave over the lights, to hide them beneath layers of shadow. But the tears were made of pure longing, and they refused to be concealed. They pushed through her fabric, appearing and disappearing as her threads passed over them.

The gods saw what happened and took pity on Stellara. "Your loneliness has created something beautiful," they told her. "These lights shall be called stars, and their twinkling will remind all who see them that even in darkness, there is beauty born from sorrow."

To this day, stars twinkle as Stellara continues her eternal weaving, her tears forever dancing between the threads of night.

Write your own myth. Use your previous myth as inspiration, but adapt it in your own way.
